=head1 NAME

LTRPipeline - Build LTR retrotransposon families from a genome with ltr-forage

=head1 SYNOPSIS

  LTRPipeline [-version] [-threads #] [-ltr_hmm <file>] [-giToID <file>]
              [-tmpdir <dir>] [-debug] <input_sequence.fa>

=head1 DESCRIPTION

Finds LTR retrotransposons in the input sequence, keeps the ones with
structural or protein evidence, and builds families from them.
RepeatModeler runs it when given -LTRStruct.

All of the work is done by one call to ltr-forage's family-library driver,
ltr_library.py:

=over 4

=item * sufr builds a suffix array of the sequence and ltr-forage finds
LTR pairs, refines their ends, annotates protein domains (nail against the
-ltr_hmm profiles), TSDs and primer binding sites, and masks tandem arrays
from the seed search.

=item * rmblastn searches of the candidates against the sequence excise
nested insertions and drop candidates far deeper than their own family
(other repeats caught between two LTRs).

=item * mmseqs/rmblastn clustering groups the elements; segmental
duplications and weakly supported singletons are dropped.

=item * te-composer builds a consensus for each cluster, separately for the
LTR and the internal region, and the models are grouped into 80-80
families with Gypsy/Copia class names.  Each model is turned to its
element's coding strand where the protein domains or the primer binding
site give it.

=item * te-composer aligns each model to its best genome copies, giving a
seed alignment whose #=GC RF line is the model unchanged.

=back

LTRPipeline then renames the models ltr-1_family-# and writes:

  <input>-ltrs.fa   ">ltr-1_family-# [ Type=LTR|INT, ltr-forage=<model>,
                     Class=<class> ]", one record per model ( an LTR
                     model and an internal model for most families )
  <input>-ltrs.stk  the models' seed alignments, rows renamed from the
                     gi-# identifiers back to the assembly's own (-giToID)
  <input>-ltrs.tsv  identifier, ltr-forage model, class, kind (LTR|INT);
                     RepeatModeler reads it when it merges the families

The working directory, with ltr_library.py's screen log ( ltr_library.log )
and its full log ( ltr_library/run.log ), is removed at the end unless
-debug is given.

The options are:

=over 4

=item -version

Displays the version of the program

=item -threads #

Number of threads for the tools the pipeline runs (default 1).

=item -ltr_hmm <file>

HMMER3 profile file for the protein-domain search.  Defaults to the one
ltr-forage ships and was validated with ( data/TEdomains.hmm, 122 Pfam
profiles of transposable-element proteins ).

=item -giToID <file>

The sequence-identifier translation file BuildDatabase writes.  Seed
alignment rows are renamed from the gi-# identifiers of the input sequence
back to the assembly's own names.  RepeatModeler passes it.

=item -tmpdir <dir>

Where to create the working directory.  Defaults to the directory of the
input sequence, then the current directory.

=item -debug

Prints the command run and keeps the working directory, with
ltr_library.py's intermediate files ( ltr_library/work ).

=back

Requires LTR_FORAGE_DIR ( ltr-forage 0.2.0 or higher, and its
ltr_library.py ), SUFR_DIR ( sufr 0.8.0 or higher ), TE_COMPOSER_DIR,
NAIL_DIR and MMseqs2.  RMBLAST_DIR is used when it holds
the Rust rmblastn ( 3.0.9 or later ); otherwise ltr_library.py finds its
own.

